course: dictionary
lesson: 12454
title: Defect: a fault, or to switch sides
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A defect is a fault or flaw. It stops something working properly or makes it look wrong. «The new kettle had a defect, so it switched off before the water boiled.» The clue is that the kettle did not work properly, so defect means a fault.
explain: A defect can also be a problem in a body part that someone is born with. «Sam was born with a small heart defect, so the doctors checked his heart every year.» The word born tells you the defect was there from the start.
explain: Defect can also be a verb, an action word. To defect means to leave your country, team or side and join the other side. «The player decided to defect to the rival team.» Leave and join are clues that the player changed sides.
explain: How do you know which meaning to use? Look at the words around it. If there is a/an, the or a name before it, it is probably a noun, like «a defect». If it follows a word like to, he or she, it is probably a verb, like «to defect». Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: A defect is a fault or flaw in something.
fact: «A defect» in a toy means the toy does not work or look right.
fact: A birth defect is a problem in a body part that someone is born with.
fact: To defect means to leave your country, team or side and join the other side.
fact: Shops may take back goods with a defect, and factories check items for defects. If 10 out of 100 items have defects, that is 10%, or 1/10 of them.
exercise: «The new kettle had a defect, so it switched off before the water boiled.» What is a defect here? | A type of cake | A happy surprise | A long walk | *A fault that stops something working properly
exercise: The shop took back the jacket because it had a defect in the zip. What does defect mean here? | A low price | A free gift | *A fault | A bright colour
exercise: «The goalkeeper decided to defect to the other club.» What does defect mean? | *To leave one team and join another | To run very fast | To sleep in the changing room | To score a goal
test: «Sam was born with a small heart defect.» What is a heart defect? | A bad mood that lasts a day | A part of the heart that is extra big | *A problem in a body part that someone is born with | A fast heartbeat after running
test: «Ten out of one hundred bikes had a defect.» What fraction of the bikes had a defect? | 10/1 | *1/10 | 1/2 | 1/100
exam: «The spy chose to defect to the other country.» What does defect mean in this sentence? | A spelling mistake in a letter | A happy holiday abroad | *To leave your country and join another | A small crack in a glass
